# ── WHAT NOT TO PUBLISH, INSIDE `public/` ONLY ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⭐⭐ THIS FILE IS NOW A BACKSTOP, NOT THE DEFENCE (F-365, 2026-08-27).
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` points `assets.directory` at `public/`, so ONLY what is inside that folder can
# be served at all. Everything else in the repo -- `worker.js`, `.dev.vars`, `scripts/`, `docs/`,
# `schema.sql`, and every scratch file anybody writes next to the code -- is unreachable by
# CONSTRUCTION rather than by an entry here that somebody remembered to add.
#
# 🔴 THAT INVERSION IS THE FIX, AND IT WAS EARNED TWICE:
#   · 2026-08-21 — `.dev.vars` was being served from the repo root. All three credentials rotated.
#   · 2026-08-27 — four probe files written beside the code were published by the next deploy,
#     one holding live share tokens. Every one returned HTTP 200 before they were noticed.
#   Both were the same fault: a DENY list only covers names somebody thought of.
#
# ⛔ SO DO NOT ADD FILES HERE TO HIDE THEM. If it must not be public, it must not be in `public/`.
# The only things that belong below are files that genuinely live inside the front end and still
# should not be served.
#
# 🔬 `node scripts/check_public_exposure.js` asks the LIVE SITE what it hands a stranger, and
# carries a positive control so it cannot pass by taking the whole site down.

# Nothing is currently excluded from `public/` -- everything in it is meant to be served.
